    "t": "3. Keyboard encoding.\n4. Data communication systems.\n5. Bus arbitration circuits.\n6. Control units.\n7. Digital controllers.\nWhat is the Difference Between Decoder and Encoder?\nS. No.\nDecoder\nEncoder\nA decoder converts binary input\ncode into one active output line.\nAn encoder converts one active\ninput line into binary output code.\nIt has n input lines and (2n)\noutput lines.\nIt has (2n) input lines and n output\nlines.\nIt performs decoding operation.\nIt performs encoding operation.\nInput is in coded binary form.\nOutput is in coded binary form.\nOnly one output line is activated\nfor each input combination.\nOnly one input line is usually active\nat a time in a normal encoder.\nExample: 3-to-8 decoder has 3\ninputs and 8 outputs.\nExample: 8-to-3 encoder has 8\ninputs and 3 outputs.\nIt is used to identify or select one\noutput line from a binary input.\nIt is used to generate binary code\ncorresponding to an active input\nline.\nIt is commonly used in memory\naddress decoding, instruction\ndecoding, and demultiplexing.\nIt is commonly used in keyboard\nencoding, priority interrupt\nsystems, and data compression.\nDecoder expands binary\ninformation.\nEncoder compresses input\ninformation into binary code.\nDecoder is the reverse operation\nof encoder.\nEncoder is the reverse operation of\ndecoder.\nApplications of Decoder:\n1. Memory address decoding: A decoder is used to select a particular\nmemory location or memory chip according to the address given by the\nCPU.\n2. Instruction decoding: In a processor, the instruction code is decoded\nto identify the operation to be performed, such as ADD, SUB, LOAD, or\nSTORE.\n3. Demultiplexing: A decoder can work as a demultiplexer by sending one\ninput signal to one selected output line.\n4. Seven-segment display: Decoders are used to convert BCD input into\nsignals required to display decimal digits on a seven-segment display.\n5. Control signal generation: Decoders generate different control signals\nrequired for digital system operations.\n6. Device selection: In digital systems, a decoder is used to select one\ndevice from many connected devices.",
