    "p": 24,
    "t": "30. The Boolean expression A + AB simplifies to:\n(a) A\n(b) B\n(c) AB\n(d) A + B\nAnswer: (a) A\n31. The Boolean expression AB + AB simplifies\nto:\n(a) A\n(b) B\n(c) AB\n(d) A + B\nAnswer: (a) A\n32. According to De Morgan’s theorem, A + B is\nequal to:\n(a) A + B\n(b) A · B\n(c) A · B\n(d) A + B\nAnswer: (b) A · B\n33. According to De Morgan’s theorem, AB is\nequal to:\n(a) A + B\n(b) A · B\n(c) A + B\n(d) AB\nAnswer: (a) A + B\n34. The dual of A + 0 = A is:\n(a) A · 1 = A\n(b) A + 1 = 1\n(c) A · 0 = 0\n(d) A + A = 1\nAnswer: (a) A · 1 = A\n35. The 1’s complement of 1011012 is:\n(a) 010010\n(b) 010011\n(c) 101010\n(d) 111111\nAnswer: (a) 010010\n36. The 2’s complement of 1011012 is:\n(a) 010010\n(b) 010011\n(c) 101010\n(d) 111111\nAnswer: (b) 010011\n37. The 2’s complement of 001011002 is:\n(a) 11010011\n(b) 11010100\n(c) 10110100\n(d) 11110100\nAnswer: (b) 11010100\n38. In sign-magnitude representation, the most sig-\nnificant bit represents:\n(a) Magnitude\n(b) Sign\n(c) Carry\n(d) Parity\nAnswer: (b) Sign\n39. In 8-bit sign-magnitude form, −25 is repre-\nsented as:\n(a) 00011001\n(b) 10011001\n(c) 11100110\n(d) 11100111\nAnswer: (b) 10011001\n40. In 8-bit 2’s complement form, −13 is repre-\nsented as:\n(a) 00001101\n(b) 10001101\n(c) 11110010\n(d) 11110011\nAnswer: (d) 11110011\n41. The range of n-bit unsigned binary numbers is:\n(a) 0 to 2n −1\n(b) −2n−1 to 2n−1 −1\n(c) 1 to 2n\n(d) −2n to 2n −1\nAnswer: (a) 0 to 2n −1\n42. The range of n-bit 2’s complement signed num-\nbers is:\n(a) 0 to 2n −1\n(b) −(2n−1 −1) to +(2n−1 −1)\n(c) −2n−1 to +(2n−1 −1)\n(d) −2n to +(2n −1)\nAnswer: (c) −2n−1 to +(2n−1 −1)\n43. The range of 8-bit 2’s complement numbers is:\n(a) 0 to 255\n(b) -127 to +127\n(c) -128 to +127\n(d) -255 to +255\nAnswer: (c) -128 to +127\n44. In 4-bit signed 2’s complement addition,\n0111 + 0001 results in:\n(a) 1000 with overflow\n(b) 1000 without overflow\n(c) 1111 with overflow\n(d) 0000 without overflow\nAnswer: (a) 1000 with overflow",
