    "p": 16,
    "t": "Computer System Architecture\nDept. of  Info. Of  Computer.\nChap. 11  Input-Output Organization\n11-16\n\n11-4  Modes of Transfer\n◆Data transfer to and from peripherals\n1) Programmed I/O\n2) Interrupt-initiated I/O\n3) Direct Memory Access (DMA)\n◆Example of Programmed I/O : Fig. 11-10, 11-11\n◆Interrupt-initiated I/O\n1) Non-vectored : fixed branch address\n2) Vectored : interrupt source supplies the branch address (interrupt vector)\nInterface\nCPU\nI/O\ndevice\nData register\nStatus\nregister\nF\nData bus\nI/O write\nI/O read\nAddress bus\nData accepted\nData valid\nI/O bus\nF = Flag bit\nRead status  register\nCheck flag bit\nRead data  register\nTransfer data to memory\nContinue\nwith\nprogram\nFlag\nOperation\ncomplete ?\n= 0\n= 1\nyes\nno",
    "ocr": false
