    "t": "Central Processing Unit\nComputer Organization\nComputer Architectures Lab\nINSTRUCTION  FORMAT\nOP-code field - specifies the operation to be performed\nAddress field - designates memory address(es) or a processor register(s)\nMode field      - determines how the address field is to be interpreted (to\nget effective address or the operand)\n• The number of address fields in the instruction format\ndepends on the internal organization of CPU\n• The three most common CPU organizations:\nInstruction Format\nSingle accumulator organization:\nADD\nX\n/* AC AC + M[X]  */\nGeneral register organization:\nADD\nR1, R2, R3\n/* R1 R2 + R3  */\nADD\nR1, R2\n/* R1 R1 + R2  */\nMOV\nR1, R2\n/* R1 R2  */\nADD\nR1, X\n/* R1 R1 + M[X]  */\nStack organization:\nPUSH\nX\n/* TOS M[X]  */\nADD\n• Instruction Fields",
