    "t": "Construct truth tables for the following:\n(a) (¬P ∧Q) →P\n(b) (P ∨Q) ∧(¬P ∨R)\n(c) (P\nQ) ∨(¬Q →R)\nDetermine whether the following are tautologies:\n(a) (P →Q) ∨(Q →P)\n(b) (P ∨Q) ∧(¬P ∨¬Q) →(P\n¬Q)\nShow that given proposition function is a tautology ((P →Q) ∧(Q→R)) →(P→R)\nEX\nR\nQ\nP\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nP →Q\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nQ→R\nT\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\n(P →Q) ∧(Q→R)\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nP→R\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nT\nF\nT\n((P →Q) ∧(Q→R)) →(P→R)\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nShow that given proposition function is a tautology ((P →Q) ∧(Q→R)) →(P→R)\nEX\n((P →Q) ∧(Q→R)) →(P→R)\nP→R\n(P →Q) ∧(Q→R)\nQ→R\nP →Q\nR\nQ\nP\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nProve that (P →Q) ⇒(¬Q →¬P ).\nA statement formula A is said to tautologically imply a statement B if and only\nif A →B is a tautology.\nIn this case we write A ⇒B, which is read as “A implies B”.\nNeed to prove (P →Q) →(¬Q →¬P ) is a tautology\nQ\nP\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\n¬P\n¬Q\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nP →Q\nT\nT\nF\nT\n(¬Q →¬P )\nT\nT\nF\nT\n(P→Q)→(¬Q→¬P)\nT\nT\nT\nT",
