    "t": "Problem 1. Convert the expression (A∧B)∨(¬A∧¬B) to DNF.\nProblem 2. Convert (¬A∨B)∧(C∨¬D) to DNF.\nEX\n1. 𝑃→\n𝑃→𝑄∧¬ ¬𝑄∨¬𝑃\nStep 1: Eliminate implications: = ¬𝑃∨\n¬𝑃∨𝑄∧¬ ¬𝑄∨¬𝑃\nStep 2: Apply De Morgan's Law: = ¬𝑃∨\n¬𝑃∨𝑄∧𝑃∧𝑄\nStep 3: Apply Distributive Law: = ¬𝑃∨\n¬𝑃∧𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑄∧𝑃∧𝑄\nStep 4: Complement Law: ¬𝑃∧𝑃= F\n= ¬𝑃∨F ∨𝑃∧𝑄\nStep 5: Identity Law: ¬𝑃∨𝑃∧𝑄\nDNF\n2. 𝑃∧¬ 𝑄∨𝑅∨\n𝑃∧𝑄∨¬𝑅∧𝑃\nStep 1: De Morgan's Law: = 𝑃∧¬𝑄∧¬𝑅∨\n𝑃∧𝑄∨¬𝑅∧𝑃\nStep 2: Distribute: = 𝑃∧¬𝑄∧¬𝑅∨\n𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑃∨¬𝑅∧𝑃\nStep 3: Idempotent Law: 𝑃∧𝑃= 𝑃\n= 𝑃∧¬𝑄∧¬𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑃∧¬𝑅\nAlready OR of AND terms.\n\n𝑃∧¬𝑄∧¬𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑃∧¬𝑅\n3. 𝑄∨𝑃∧𝑅\n∧\n𝑃∨𝑅∧𝑄\nStep 1: Rearrange :  =\n𝑄∨𝑃∧𝑅\n∧𝑄∧𝑃∨𝑅\nStep 2: Distribute : =\n𝑄∧𝑄∨\n𝑃∧𝑅∧𝑄\n∧𝑃∨𝑅\nStep 3: Idempotent Law : = 𝑄∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅\n∧𝑃∨𝑅\nStep 4: Distribute: = 𝑄∧𝑃∨𝑅\n∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅∧𝑃∨𝑅\nStep 5: Distribute first term: = 𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑄∧𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅∧𝑃∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅∧𝑅\nStep 6: Idempotent Law: = 𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑄∧𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅\n𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑄∧𝑅∨𝑃∧𝑄∧𝑅\n(This is a valid DNF. If simplification is allowed later, it reduces to 𝑃∧𝑄∨𝑄∧𝑅.)",
