    "t": "Example 1 (Negation + Implication)\nConvert into CNF:\n¬(𝑝→𝑞∨𝑟)\nSolution\nFirst eliminate implication:\n𝑝→𝑞∨𝑟≡¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\nSo:\n¬ ¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\nApply De Morgan’s law:\n¬ ¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟≡𝑝∧¬𝑞∧¬𝑟\nFinal CNF:\n𝑝∧¬𝑞∧¬𝑟\nThis is CNF (AND of clauses, each clause has\none literal).\nExample 2 (Nested Structure)\nConvert into DNF:\n𝑝∨𝑞∧𝑟∨¬𝑞\nSolution\nApply distributive law:\n𝑝∧𝑟∨𝑝∧¬𝑞∨𝑞∧𝑟∨𝑞∧¬𝑞\nEliminate contradiction:\n𝑞∧¬𝑞= 𝐹\nFinal DNF:\n𝑝∧𝑟∨𝑝∧¬𝑞∨𝑞∧𝑟\n\nProper DNF: OR of ANDs.\nExample 3 (Biconditional)\nConvert into CNF:\n𝑝\n𝑞\nSolution\nReplace biconditional:\n𝑝→𝑞∧𝑞→𝑝\nReplace implications:\n¬𝑝∨𝑞∧¬𝑞∨𝑝\nFinal CNF:\n¬𝑝∨𝑞∧¬𝑞∨𝑝\n\nClassic CNF form.\nExample 4 (Negation over Biconditional)\nConvert into DNF:\n¬ 𝑝\n𝑞\nSolution\nBy definition, the biconditional is:\n𝑝\n𝑞   ≡   𝑝→𝑞∧𝑞→𝑝\nSo the given expression becomes:\n¬[ 𝑝→𝑞∧𝑞→𝑝]\n¬[ ¬𝑝∨𝑞∧¬𝑞∨𝑝]\nUse identity:\n¬ 𝑝\n𝑞≡𝑝∧¬𝑞∨¬𝑝∧𝑞\nFinal DNF:\n𝑝∧¬𝑞∨¬𝑝∧𝑞\n\nAlready in perfect DNF.\nExample 5 (Three variables + implication) - Convert into CNF: 𝑝∧𝑞→𝑟\nExample 6 (Mixed operators) - Convert into DNF:   ¬ 𝑝∨𝑞∧𝑟\nExample 7 (CNF vs DNF ) - Is the following CNF, DNF, both, or neither? - 𝑝∨𝑞\nExample 8 (Not in either form) - Convert into CNF: 𝑝∨𝑞→𝑟\n5 :\n¬𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟\nSingle clause →valid CNF.\n6 :\n¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∨¬𝑝∧¬𝑟\n7 ?:  𝑝∨𝑞\nAnswer:\nCorrect answer: Both CNF and DNF\nSingle disjunction of literals  ->\nValid CNF (one clause)  |\nValid DNF (one term)\n8 :\n¬𝑝∨𝑟∧¬𝑞∨𝑟\nA minterm represents one exact situation (one row of the truth table) where the formula is TRUE.\nThink of it as: “This AND-expression is true in only one specific assignment of truth values.”\nFormal Definition - A minterm is a conjunction (AND) of all the variables in the formula, where\neach variable appears exactly once, either in its original form or negated, but not both.\nHow to form a minterm (Rule)\nFor a given truth-table row:\nIf the variable is True (T) →write it without negation\nIf the variable is False (F) →write it with negation\nMIN TERM\nMinterm\nq\np\np∧q\nT\nT\np∧¬q\nF\nT\n¬p∧q\nT\nF\n¬p∧¬q\nF\nF\nr\nq\np\nT\nF\nT\nFor p, q, r one minterm example  ????\nMinterm:             𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟",
