    "t": "A maxterm represents one exact situation (one row of the truth table) where the formula is FALSE.\nThink of it as: “This OR-expression is false in only one specific assignment.”\nFormal Definition  - A maxterm is a disjunction (OR) of all the variables in the formula, where each\nvariable appears exactly once, either in its original form or negated, but not both.\nHow to form a maxterm (Rule)\nFor a given truth-table row:\nIf the variable is True (T) → write it negated\nIf the variable is False (F) → write it without negation\n\n Note: This is the opposite of minterm construction.\nMAXTERM\nMaxterm\nq\np\n¬p∨¬q\nT\nT\n¬p∨q\nF\nT\np∨¬q\nT\nF\np∨q\nF\nF\nr\nq\np\nF\nT\nF\nFor p, q, r one maxterm example  ????\nMaxterm:             𝑝 ∨ ¬𝑞 ∨ 𝑟\nMaxterm\nMinterm\nOR (∨) of literals\nAND (∧) of literals\nRepresents FALSE row\nRepresents TRUE row\nUsed in PCNF\nUsed in PDNF\nLiteral is opposite of value\nLiteral matches value\nMemory Trick\nMinterm → Match the value\nMaxterm → Make it opposite\n Final One-Line Definitions (Perfect for Exams)\n•Minterm: A conjunction of all variables, each appearing exactly once, that is true for exactly one truth-table\nrow.\n•Maxterm: A disjunction of all variables, each appearing exactly once, that is false for exactly one truth-table\nrow.\nALL MINTERM AND MAXTERM FOR 3 VARIABLES\nMaxterm (PCNF)\nMinterm (PDNF)\nr\nq\np\nNo.\np ∨q ∨r\n¬p ∧¬q ∧¬r\nF\nF\nF\np ∨q ∨¬r\n¬p ∧¬q ∧r\nT\nF\nF\np ∨¬q ∨r\n¬p ∧q ∧¬r\nF\nT\nF\np ∨¬q ∨¬r\n¬p ∧q ∧r\nT\nT\nF\n¬p ∨q ∨r\np ∧¬q ∧¬r\nF\nF\nT\n¬p ∨q ∨¬r\np ∧¬q ∧r\nT\nF\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨r\np ∧q ∧¬r\nF\nT\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨¬r\np ∧q ∧r\nT\nT\nT\nMaxterm (PCNF)\nMinterm (PDNF)\ns\nr\nq\np\nNo.\nP ∨q ∨r ∨s\n¬p ∧¬q ∧¬r ∧¬s\nF\nF\nF\nF\nP ∨q ∨r ∨¬s\n¬p ∧¬q ∧¬r ∧s\nT\nF\nF\nF\nP ∨q ∨¬r ∨s\n¬p ∧¬q ∧r ∧¬s\nF\nT\nF\nF\nP ∨q ∨¬r ∨¬s\n¬p ∧¬q ∧r ∧s\nT\nT\nF\nF\nP ∨¬q ∨r ∨s\n¬p ∧q ∧¬r ∧¬s\nF\nF\nT\nF\nP ∨¬q ∨r ∨¬s\n¬p ∧q ∧¬r ∧s\nT\nF\nT\nF\nP ∨¬q ∨¬r ∨s\n¬p ∧q ∧r ∧¬s\nF\nT\nT\nF\nP ∨¬q ∨¬r ∨¬s\n¬p ∧q ∧r ∧s\nT\nT\nT\nF\n¬p ∨q ∨r ∨s\nP ∧¬q ∧¬r ∧¬s\nF\nF\nF\nT\n¬p ∨q ∨r ∨¬s\nP ∧¬q ∧¬r ∧s\nT\nF\nF\nT\n¬p ∨q ∨¬r ∨s\nP ∧¬q ∧r ∧¬s\nF\nT\nF\nT\n¬p ∨q ∨¬r ∨¬s\nP ∧¬q ∧r ∧s\nT\nT\nF\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨r ∨s\nP ∧q ∧¬r ∧¬s\nF\nF\nT\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨r ∨¬s\nP ∧q ∧¬r ∧s\nT\nF\nT\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨¬r ∨s\nP ∧q ∧r ∧¬s\nF\nT\nT\nT\n¬p ∨¬q ∨¬r ∨¬s\nP ∧q ∧r ∧s\nT\nT\nT\nT\nALL MINTERM AND MAXTERM FOR 4 VARIABLES",
