    "p": 47,
    "t": "Find the DNF and CNF of the formula using Truth Table  ¬𝑝→𝑟   ∧   𝑝\n𝑞\n(¬p →r) ∧(p\nq)\np\nq\n¬p →r\n¬p\nr\nq\np\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nThe formula is TRUE in the following rows:\n1. p = T, q = T, r = T →𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟\n2. p = T, q = T, r = F →𝑝∧𝑞∧¬𝑟\n3. p = F, q = F, r = T →¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟\nObtain the DNF (from TRUE rows)\nFinal DNF\n𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟   ∨   𝑝∧𝑞∧¬𝑟   ∨   ¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟\n(¬p →r) ∧(p\nq)\np\nq\n¬p →r\n¬p\nr\nq\np\nT\nT\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nT\nT\nT\nT\nT\nF\nF\nF\nT\nF\nT\nF\nF\nF\nFinal CNF\n¬𝑝∨𝑞∨¬𝑟   ∧   ¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟   ∧   𝑝∨¬𝑞∨¬𝑟   ∧   𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟   ∧   𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\nObtain the CNF (from FALSE rows)\nThe formula is FALSE in the following\nrows:\n•\n(T, F, T)\n•\n(T, F, F)\n•\n(F, T, T)\n•\n(F, T, F)\n•\n(F, F, F)\nFor each false row, we write a maxterm:\nCorresponding maxterms\n1. (T, F, T) →¬𝑝∨𝑞∨¬𝑟\n2. (T, F, F) →¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\n3. (F, T, T) →𝑝∨¬𝑞∨¬𝑟\n4. (F, T, F) →𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟\n5. (F, F, F) →𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\nRule for maxterm:\n•Variable = T → write its negation\n•Variable = F → write it unnegated\nExample 1 - Find DNF and CNF of: 𝑝→𝑞∧𝑟\nTruth table →TRUE rows:  T,T,T →𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟\n|          F,T,T →¬𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟\n| F,F,T →¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟\nDNF:                                        𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟∨¬𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟∨¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟\nCNF (from FALSE rows):   ¬𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟∧¬𝑝∨𝑞∨¬𝑟∧¬𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟∧𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟∧𝑝∨𝑞∨𝑟\nExample 2 - Find DNF and CNF of: ¬ 𝑝∧𝑞∨𝑟\nSimplification: ¬𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟\nDNF: ¬𝑝   ∨   ¬𝑞   ∨  𝑟\nCNF: ¬𝑝∨¬𝑞∨𝑟- single clause →both CNF & DNF)\nExample 3 - Find DNF and CNF of: 𝑝\n𝑞∧𝑟\nTRUE rows:\np=T, q=T, r=T\np=F, q=F, r=F\np=F, q=F, r=T\nDNF: 𝑝∧𝑞∧𝑟   ∨   ¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧¬𝑟   ∨   ¬𝑝∧¬𝑞∧𝑟\nCNF: ¬𝑝∨𝑞∧¬𝑝∨𝑟∧𝑝∨¬𝑞∨¬𝑟\nA formula is in Principal Disjunctive Normal Form (PDNF) if it is written as a disjunction (OR) of\nminterms, and each minterm contains every variable exactly once, either in negated or\nunnegated form.\nThink of PDNF as:\n“Write down all the exact situations (truth assignments) where the formula is TRUE, and OR them together.”\nPDNF – Step-by-Step Method\nStep 1 : Construct the truth table of the given formula.\nStep 2: Identify all rows where the formula is TRUE.\nStep 3: For each such row, write the corresponding minterm.\nStep 4: Take the OR of all those minterms →this is the PDNF.\nPRINCIPAL DISJUNCTIVE NORMAL FORM (PDNF)",
