    "t": "Problem\nCheck the validity of the following argument:\nIf the network is secure, then data is encrypted.\nIf data is encrypted, then the system is safe.\nThe system is not safe.\nConclusion:\nThe network is not secure.\nLet\n• p: The network is secure\n• q: Data is encrypted\n• r: The system is safe\nPremises\n1. 𝑝→𝑞\n2. 𝑞→𝑟\n3. ¬𝑟\nProof\n4. 𝑝→𝑟\n(Hypothetical Syllogism using 1,2)\n5. ¬𝑝\n(Modus Tollens using 4,3)\nConclusion\n∴  ¬𝑝\nThe network is not secure.\nProblem\nCheck the validity of the following argument:\nIf the network is secure, then data is encrypted.\nIf data is encrypted, then the system is safe.\nThe system is not safe.\nConclusion:\nThe network is not secure.\nLet\n• p: The network is secure\n• q: Data is encrypted\n• r: The system is safe\nPremises\n1. 𝑝→𝑞\n2. 𝑞→𝑟\n3. ¬𝑟\nProof\n4. 𝑝→𝑟\n(Hypothetical Syllogism using 1,2)\n5. ¬𝑝\n(Modus Tollens using 4,3)\nConclusion\n∴  ¬𝑝\nThe network is not secure.\nProblem 5\nGiven statements:\nRam is intelligent and hardworking.\nConclusion:\nRam is intelligent.\nSolution\nLet:\np: Ram is intelligent\nq: Ram is hardworking\nPremise:\n𝑝∧𝑞\nStep: 𝑝\n(Simplification)\nConclusion: 𝑝\nProblem 6\nGiven statements:\n•\nJohn has a laptop.\n•\nJohn has internet access.\nConclusion:\nJohn has a laptop and internet access.\nSolution\nLet:\n• p: John has a laptop\n• q: John has internet access\nPremises:    𝟏.   𝑝\n2.     𝑞\nStep:    𝑝∧𝑞\n(Conjunction)\nConclusion: 𝑝∧𝑞\nProblem 7\nGiven statements:\nIf it is raining, then the ground is wet.\nIf the ground is wet, then the match is\ncancelled.\nIt is raining.\nConclusion:\nThe match is cancelled.\nSolution\nLet:\np: It is raining\nq: Ground is wet\nr: Match is cancelled\nPremises:\n𝑝→𝑞\n𝑞→𝑟\n𝑝\nSteps:\n𝑝→𝑟\n(Hypothetical Syllogism)\n𝑟\n(Modus Ponens)\nConclusion: 𝑟\nProblem 8\nGiven statements:\n•\nIf the system crashes, then data is lost.\n•\nIf data is lost, then the backup fails.\n•\nThe backup did not fail.\nConclusion:\nThe system did not crash.\nSolution\nLet:\n•p: System crashes\n•q: Data is lost\n•r: Backup fails\nPremises:\n1.𝑝→𝑞\n2.𝑞→𝑟\n3.¬𝑟\nSteps:\n𝑝→𝑟\n(Hypothetical Syllogism)\n¬𝑝\n(Modus Tollens)\nConclusion: ¬𝑝",
