    "p": 5,
    "t": "The correct idea for additive inverse in Z4 is:\n▪A + b ≡ 0(mod4)\n▪In other words: The inverse of a is the element which, when added to a, gives 0 modulo 4.\n▪For example:\n▪Inverse of 0 → 0 + 0 = 0\n▪Inverse of 1 → 1 + 3 = 4 ≡ 0 (mod 4)\n▪Inverse of 2 → 2 + 2 = 4 ≡ 0 (mod 4)\n▪Inverse of 3 → 3 + 1 = 4 ≡ 0(mod 4)\n“An additive inverse is the number that brings the sum back to the identity element 0.”",
