    "t": "A subset H of a group G is called a subgroups of G if\ni)\nwhenever a 𝜖 H , b 𝜖 H . The product ab 𝜖 H\nii)\ne 𝜖 H\niii)\nFor each a 𝜖 H its inverse 𝑎 −1 in G also belongs to H.\nA non empty subset H of a group G is called a subgroup of G if H itself form a group with respect\nto the binary operation defined in G.\nExample: The group of integer under addition forms a subgroup of G.\nSUB GROUP",
