    "t": "Frequency\nLetter\nS\nT\nI\nA\nC\nQ11. Distinct permutations of \"STATISTICS\"\nLet's count the letters carefully.\nSTATISTICS\nTotal letters: 10\nFrequency:\nTherefore:\n10!\n3! 3! 2!\nCalculate:\n10! = 3,628,800\n3!3! 2! = 6 × 6 × 2 = 72\nTherefore:\n3,628,800\n50,400\nAnswer:  50,400\nQ12. Distinct permutations of \"STATISTICS\" begin\nand end with S\nWe have 3 S’s.  We require:       𝑆 _ _ _ _ _ _ _ 𝑆\nUse two S's at the beginning and end.\nRemaining letters:\n•\nS →1\n•\nT →3\n•\nI →2\n•\nA →1\n•\nC →1\nSo 8 letters remain.\nNumber of arrangements:\n8!\n3! 2!\nWhy?\nBecause among the remaining 8 letters:\n•\nT occurs 3 times\n•\nI occurs 2 times\nTherefore:\n40320\n6 × 2\n= 40320\n3360\nAnswer:\n3360\nQ13. 10 football games\nThe team plays:\n•\n5 wins\n•\n4 losses\n•\n1 tie\nTotal:  5 + 4 + 1 = 10\nWe need to arrange the results:\n𝑊, 𝑊, 𝑊, 𝑊, 𝑊, 𝐿, 𝐿, 𝐿, 𝐿, 𝑇\nThe same result is repeated.\nTherefore:\n10!\n5! 4! 1!\n= 3,628,800\n120 × 24\n= 3,628,800\n2880\n1260\nAnswer: 1260\nQ14. Dinner orders\nThere are 8 people:\n•\n3 order chicken\n•\n4 order steak\n•\n1 orders lobster\nSo we arrange:\n𝐶, 𝐶, 𝐶, 𝑆, 𝑆, 𝑆, 𝑆, 𝐿\nNumber of ways:\n8!\n3! 4! 1!\n= 40320\n6 × 24\n= 40320\nAnswer: 280",
