    "t": "Permutation formula is used to find the number of ways to pick ‘r’ things out of ‘n’ different\nthings in a specific order, and replacement is not allowed.\nThe formula is given as follows:\nIn general, n distinct things can be set taking r (r < n) at a time in n(n - 1)(n - 2)...(n - r - 1) ways.\nIn fact, the first thing can be any of the n things.\nAs a particular case of this, we get P(n, n) = n!\nThat is the number of different arrangements (Permutations) of n distinct objects.\nPERMUTATION FORMULA\nWe have 𝑛objects in total, but some are repeated:\n𝑛ଵare of the first type,\n𝑛ଶare of the second type,\n…,\n𝑛௞are of the 𝑘-th type.\nand 𝑛ଵ+ 𝑛ଶ+ ⋯+ 𝑛௞= 𝑛.\nFormula: The number of distinct permutations is\n𝑛!\n𝑛ଵ!ࣟ𝑛ଶ!ࣟ⋯ࣟ𝑛௞! .\nWhy?\nIf all objects were distinct →𝑛! permutations.\nBut since 𝑛ଵobjects are identical, swapping them doesn’t create a new arrangement, so we\ndivide by 𝑛ଵ!.\nSimilarly divide by 𝑛ଶ!, 𝑛ଷ!, … , 𝑛௞!.\nExample\nWord BALLOON\nTotal letters: 𝑛= 7.\nMultiplicities: L=2, O=2, others single.\nSo, ଻!\nଶ!ࣟଶ! = ହ଴ସ଴\nସ\n= 1260\ndistinct permutations.\nFinal Answer: Number of permutations =\n௡!\n௡భ!ࣟ௡మ!ࣟ⋯ࣟ௡ೖ!",
