    "t": "Example 1: Word “MISSISSIPPI”\nTotal letters 𝑛= 11.\nFrequencies:\nM = 1\nI = 4\nS = 4\nP = 2\nPermutations =\nଵଵ!\nଵ!ࣟସ!ࣟସ!ࣟଶ! = ଷଽଽଵ଺଼଴଴\nଵଵହଶ\n= 34650\nExample 3: Arranging colored balls\nSuppose you have 10 balls: 3 red, 4 blue, 3 green.\nTotal 𝑛= 10.\nFrequencies: 𝑛ଵ= 3, 𝑛ଶ= 4, 𝑛ଷ= 3.\nPermutations =\n10!\n3!ࣟ4!ࣟ3! = 3628800\n= 4200\nExample 4: Word “COMMITTEE”\nTotal letters 𝑛= 9.\nFrequencies:\nC = 1\nO = 1\nM = 2\nI = 1\nT = 2\nE = 2\nPermutations =\n9!\n2!ࣟ2!ࣟ2! = 362880\n= 45360\nExample 5: Simple numeric case\nArrange digits of 1122.\nTotal 𝑛= 4.\nFrequencies: 1 appears twice, 2 appears twice.\n4!\n2!ࣟ2! = 24\n4 = 6\nThe actual distinct permutations are:\n\n1122, 1212, 1221, 2112, 2121, 2211.",
