    "t": "(a) There are only aces or face cards\nStep 1: Count the available cards\nThere are:\n•\n4 Aces\n•\n12 face cards (J, Q, K)\nSo total available cards:  4 + 12 = 16\nWe have to choose 5 cards from these 16.\nTherefore:\nଵ଺𝐶ହ\nUsing the formula:\n௡𝐶௥=\n௡!\n௥! ௡ି௥!\nଵ଺𝐶ହ= 16!\n5! 11!\n= ଵ଺×ଵହ×ଵସ×ଵଷ×ଵଶ\nହ×ସ×ଷ×ଶ×ଵ\n= 4368\nAnswer: 4368\n(b) There are only numbered cards (no letters)\nThe number cards are:   2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,10\nThere are 9 number cards in each suit.\nSince there are 4 suits:   9 × 4 = 36\nSo we have 36 numbered cards.\nChoose any 5:\nଷ଺𝐶ହ\n= 36!\n5!31!\n= 36 × 35 × 34 × 33 × 32\n5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1\n= 376,992\nAnswer: 376,992\n(c) There are 2 clubs and 3 diamonds\nWe need: 2 clubs AND 3 diamonds\nThere are 13 clubs and 13 diamonds.\nStep 1: Choose 2 clubs from 13\nଵଷ𝐶ଶ=   =\nଵଷ×ଵଶ\nଶ\n= 78\nStep 2: Choose 3 diamonds from 13\nଵଷ𝐶ଷ=  =\nଵଷ×ଵଶ×ଵଵ\nଷ×ଶ×ଵ\n=   = 286\nStep 3: Multiply\nThe club selection and diamond selection are independent:\nଵଷ𝐶ଶ×\nଵଷ𝐶ଷ          =   = 78 × 286\n=       = 22,308\nAnswer:  22,308\n(d) There are at least 4 red cards\nWhat does \"at least 4\" mean?\nAt least 4 means:\n4 or more\nSince we are selecting 5 cards, the possibilities\nare:\nCase 1: Exactly 4 red cards\nChoose 4 red cards from 26:\nଶ଺𝐶ସ\nThe remaining 1 card must be black:\nଶ଺𝐶ଵ\nTherefore:\nଶ଺𝐶ସ\nଶ଺𝐶ଵ\nCase 2: Exactly 5 red cards\nChoose all 5 cards from the 26 red cards:\nଶ଺𝐶ହ\nTherefore:\nଶ଺𝐶ସ\nଶ଺𝐶ଵ+\nଶ଺𝐶ହ\nNow calculate.\nଶ଺𝐶ସ= 14,950\nand\nଶ଺𝐶ଵ= 26\nSo:\n14,950 × 26\n= 388,700\nAlso:\nଶ଺𝐶ହ= 65,780\nTherefore:\n388,700 + 65,780\n= 454,480\nAnswer: 454,480",
