    "t": "Computer Network Architecture\nVarious special graphs play an important role in the design of computer networks.\n\nSome local area networks use a star topology, which is a complete bipartite graph K1,n ,as shown in (a). All devices are\nconnected to a central control device.\n\nOther local networks are based on a ring topology, where each device is connected to exactly two  others using Cn ,as\nillustrated in (b). Messages may be sent around the ring.\n\nOthers, as illustrated in (c), use a Wn – based topology, combining the features of a star topology and a ring topology.\n\nVarious special graphs also play a role in parallel processing where processors need to be interconnected as one processor\nmay need the output generated by another.\n\n The n-dimensional hypercube, or n-cube, Qn, is a common way to connect processors in parallel, e.g., Intel Hypercube.\n\nAnother common method is the mesh network, illustrated here                                                  for 16 processors.",
